.TH ADRAW 2
.SH NAME
scrollinit, scrolldraw, scrollmouse, scrollwid, scrollgap \- helpers for programs that draw an acme window
.SH SYNOPSIS
.ta \w'void 'u
.B #include <u.h>
.br
.B #include <libc.h>
.br
.B #include <draw.h>
.br
.B #include <thread.h>
.br
.B #include <mouse.h>
.br
.B #include <adraw.h>
.PP
.ft L
.nf
typedef struct Scroll Scroll;
struct Scroll
{
	Rectangle	r;
	vlong	tot;
	vlong	p0;
	vlong	p1;
	Image	*back;
	Image	*bord;
};
.fi
.PP
.B
void	scrollinit(Scroll *s)
.PP
.B
void	scrolldraw(Image *dst, Scroll *s)
.PP
.B
void	scrollmouse(Mousectl *mc, Scroll *s, void (*set)(Scroll *s, vlong p0, void *a), void *a)
.PP
.B
int	scrollwid(void)
.PP
.B
int	scrollgap(void)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Libadraw
holds helpers for a program that draws the body of an
.IR acme (1)
window, as
.IR chess (1)
does.
A program uses those it wants; none of them needs the others,
and none opens a window or reads its events.
.PP
A
.B Scroll
is a scroll bar that looks and works as acme's own.
.B r
is where it is drawn,
.B tot
the size of what it scrolls, in any unit,
and
.B p0
and
.B p1
the part of it that shows.
.I Scrollinit
gives it acme's colors from the theme
.RI ( theme (6)):
.BR body 's
back for the part that shows and
.B bodyborder
for the rest.
.I Scrolldraw
draws it in
.IR dst .
.I Scrollwid
and
.I Scrollgap
are acme's width for a scroll bar and the gap after it, scaled for the display.
.PP
.I Scrollmouse
works the bar while a button pressed in it is held, as acme does:
button 1 moves back and button 3 forward, by as much of what shows as the pointer is
down the bar; button 2 moves to the place the pointer is at; and buttons 1 and 3 repeat
while held, after a pause.
Each time it moves,
.I scrollmouse
sets
.B p0
and
.B p1
and calls
.IR set ,
with
.IR a ,
to draw what shows from
.BR p0 .
The program moves for the mouse wheel itself.
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/libadraw
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR acme (1),
.IR chess (1),
.IR theme (6)
